<h1>xor</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
"Exclusive OR" or "not equal to" function:  0 XOR 0 = 0, 0 XOR 1 = 1, 1 XOR 0 = 1, 1 XOR 1 = 0.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> exclusive or.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="and.html"><em>and</em></a>, <a href="or.html"><em>or</em></a>, <a href="not.html"><em>not</em></a>, <a href="implies.html"><em>implies</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The name "exclusive or" is in contrast with inclusive <a href="or.html"><em>or</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

